# ============================================================================
# BEAM Light Wallet - Git Ignore
# Developed by @vsnation
# ============================================================================

# =============================================================================
# BINARIES - Downloaded from BEAM releases (large files)
# =============================================================================
binaries/linux/*
binaries/macos/*
binaries/windows/*
!binaries/linux/.gitkeep
!binaries/macos/.gitkeep
!binaries/windows/.gitkeep

# =============================================================================
# WALLET DATA - Contains sensitive private keys!
# =============================================================================
wallets/*/
!wallets/.gitkeep

# =============================================================================
# NODE DATA - Blockchain database (very large)
# =============================================================================
node_data/
node.db
*.db
!config/*.json

# =============================================================================
# LOGS
# =============================================================================
logs/*
!logs/.gitkeep
*.log

# =============================================================================
# BUILD ARTIFACTS
# =============================================================================
build/*.dmg
build/*.app/
build/*.iconset/
build/*.icns
build/*.png
!build/AppIcon.svg
!build/beam-logo.svg

# Windows build artifacts
build/windows/*.exe
build/windows/Output/

# =============================================================================
# STATE FILES - Runtime state (regenerated)
# =============================================================================
.wallet_status.json
.active_wallet
.node_mode
.webserver.pid
.wallet_api.pid
.node.pid
*.pid

# =============================================================================
# ARCHIVES
# =============================================================================
*.tar.gz
*.tar
*.zip
*.dmg

# =============================================================================
# PYTHON
# =============================================================================
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
venv/
env/
.env

# =============================================================================
# OS FILES
# =============================================================================
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# =============================================================================
# IDE / EDITORS
# =============================================================================
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*.sublime-workspace
*.sublime-project
.project
.settings/
.classpath
*.iml

# =============================================================================
# TEMP FILES
# =============================================================================
*.tmp
*.temp
*.bak
*.backup
*~

# =============================================================================
# SECRETS - Never commit these!
# =============================================================================
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
.env
.env.local
secrets/
credentials/
node-utxo-image.bin
.wallet_config
CLAUDE.md
.owner_key

# =============================================================================
# PROJECT FILES NOT FOR RELEASE
# =============================================================================
# Fuddle word lists (large, not part of wallet)
data/fuddle/

# Contract sources ARE tracked. The compiled .wasm in shaders/ hold real user
# funds; without the source nobody — including us, after a disk failure — can
# rebuild or audit them. Word lists stay out (see below).
contracts/**/words_*.txt

# Word lists (game answers - NEVER share publicly)
fuddle_words_push/
data/fuddle/
**/words_*.txt

# Marketing & tooling scripts
# Local tooling: marketing automation, deploy helpers, and the word-list
# seeders whose answers must stay private. Ignore the contents rather than the
# directory itself, so specific files can be un-ignored below - git cannot
# un-ignore a file inside an excluded directory.
scripts/*
# ...except the release verification tooling, which users must be able to fetch.
!scripts/check_dapp_packages.sh
!scripts/release-sign.sh
!scripts/verify-release.sh

# Test files are tracked. They used to carry a real mainnet wallet password,
# which is why they were ignored; they now read $BEAM_TEST_PASSWORD instead.
tests/screenshots/
tests/**/*.png

# Internal documentation
ARCHITECTURE.md
FUDDLE.md
HOW_THE_E2E_CHAT_WORKS.md
HOW_TO_DO_SHADERS_ON_BEAM.md
IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
KNOWLEDGE.md
P2P_FIXES_TRACKER.md
P2P_IMPLEMENTATION.md
P2P_IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md
P2P_STATUS_REPORT.md
P2P_TESTING_README.md
P2P_TEST_CHECKLIST.md
P2P_TEST_RESULTS.md
PLAN.md
X_MARKETING_PLAN.md

# P2P data
p2p_data/

# Media files
gifs/
screenshots/

# Duplicate install scripts in root
macos_install.sh
linux_install.sh
windows_install.bat

# Build output (DMG, app bundles, releases)
build/macos/*.dmg
build/macos/BEAM Light Wallet.app/
build/macos/AppIcon.icns
build/macos/AppIcon.svg.png
build/releases/

# Data directory (runtime)
data/

# Third-party Stadium web app kept alongside for reference; not part of the
# wallet. 152 MB of videos and build artifacts once got swept in by `git add -A`
# and had to be filtered back out of an unpushed branch.
meme_game/

# Agent tooling. Contains credentials and internal notes; never ship it.
.claude/

# The signing PRIVATE key must never be here. The public key is committed
# deliberately by the maintainer once they generate their own keypair.
*-release-key.pem
.beam-release-key.pem

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal documents. Not secret, but not for other people either - and one of
# them is actively dangerous to publish.
#
# PRODUCTISATION_PLAN.md is a written vulnerability report: "any website can
# spend the user's funds", "XSS from a received transaction", "DELETE destroys
# every wallet". All fixed in 1.2.x - but anyone still on 1.0.x is unpatched,
# so publishing it hands an attacker a step-by-step guide aimed at them.
#
# P2P_REWORK.md states that a feature flag is the only thing between ~10,000
# lines of disabled code and users, which is a map of where to push.
#
# The rest are business material and admin runbooks: marketing plans, scheduled
# promo posts, deployment steps and contract admin keys.
#
# NOTE: ignoring a file does not unpublish it. These are already on GitHub and
# remain in history; this only stops further changes going out.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/PRODUCTISATION_PLAN.md
docs/P2P_REWORK.md
contracts/DEPLOYMENT.md
contracts/p2p_escrow/DEPLOYMENT.md
memeclash/marketing.md
memeclash/prewarmup_posts.md
memeclash/memory.md
memeclash/deploy_tokens.md
